<article class="env-lemma" id="04NZ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04NZ">Lemma <span data-tag="04NZ">67.45.9</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. The following are equivalent </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$f$ is finite, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$f$ is affine and proper. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      In both cases the morphism is representable, and you can check the condition after base change to an affine scheme mapping into $Y$, see Lemmas <a href="/tag/03ZQ" data-tag="03ZQ">67.45.3</a>, <a href="/tag/03WG" data-tag="03WG">67.20.3</a>, and <a href="/tag/083R" data-tag="083R">67.40.2</a>. Hence the result follows from Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/01WN" data-tag="01WN">29.45.11</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>